<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # I'm Outside. I'm Happy! – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 3rd Grade (CEFR: A1.1)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> I Can Connect with Nature!</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> I'm Outside. I'm Happy!</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Communication: Assist peers in following oral directions. Concept: Explain simple events in story form.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can assist peers in following nature-related directions with simple gestures (e.g., pointing to a tree and saying, "Sit by the tree."). Can explain simple nature events with gestures (e.g., "The sun shines," and points to a sun). Can help peers understand steps in a nature story by pointing and saying basic words (e.g., "Now find a tree.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Nature Sounds Guessing Game. The teacher plays short audio clips of nature sounds (e.g., bird singing, water flowing in a stream, wind blowing through trees). Students listen and guess the sound, saying simple words like "bird!" or "water!".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models explaining one sound with a simple sentence and gesture. "I hear a *bird* (points to ear, then mimics bird flying). A bird can *sing*." The teacher also models pointing to a picture of the sun and saying, "The *sun* shines. I'm *happy* outside." The teacher emphasizes the /k/ sound in "can" and the /s/ sound in "sun" while modeling.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding using simple questions and gestures.
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can we hear a *fish* (mimics swimming) *sing*?" (Students shake heads for "No.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is the *sun* in the *sky* (points up) or on the *grass* (points down)?" (Students point up for "Sky.")</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "I Can Connect with Nature!".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A simple illustrated picture story sequence (4-5 frames) displayed on flashcards or a projector, showing a child's short walk in a nature spot. Each frame has a very short, simple caption. Example sequence:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Frame 1: Child walking to a park entrance. Caption: "I *walk* to the *park*."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Frame 2: Child looking at a flower. Caption: "I *see* a *flower*."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Frame 3: Child sitting under a tree. Caption: "I sit *by* the *tree*."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Frame 4: Child listening to birds. Caption: "I *hear* a *bird*."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Frame 5: Child smiling happily. Caption: "I'm *happy* *outside*."</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Explaining simple events in story form. Talking about sensory observations and experiences in nature (e.g., "I hear the birds." "The flowers smell nice.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> The teacher shows the pictures in a scrambled order.
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Questions:</b> "What is the boy doing?" (Exploring nature/walking). "Is he inside or outside?" (Outside).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Ordering:</b> "What happens first? Show me number 1." (Students point or raise fingers). "What happens next?" (Students put the pictures in the correct sequence as a class activity).</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Can/Can't, Prepositions of place (in, by, near, under), Present simple (I walk, I see, I hear, I am).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> tree, grass, flower, bird, park, sun, walk, listen, look, see, happy, outside.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Practice /k/ in "can" and /s/ in "sun". Blending /s/ /ʌ/ /n/ to "sun", /f/ /l/ /ɑʊ/ /ɚ/ to "flower".</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic:</b> Locating people and things; Expressing connection with nature.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion with Actions):</b> The teacher shows flashcards of nature items (e.g., *tree*, *flower*, *bird*, *sun*). Students complete sentences orally, performing simple actions. "I can see a ____." (Students say "tree" and point to the tree picture). "I can hear a ____." (Students say "bird" and cup their ear). Teacher guides to use "can" and specific words. Teacher ensures pronunciation of /k/ and /s/ is clear.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Guided Story Retelling with Peer Gestures):</b> In pairs, students retell a simplified version of the Stage 2 story. Partner A says a simple sentence from the story (e.g., "I walk to the park."). Partner B listens and uses gestures to help Partner A or another peer understand the action (e.g., walking motion, pointing to a 'park' area). Then they switch roles. Teacher prompts: "Can you show your friend?" and "Where is the flower?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Explain the Nature Spot):</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher provides each pair with a simple drawing of a nature spot (e.g., a *park* with a *tree*, a *river*, a *picnic* blanket, a *flower*, a *bird*). Partner A points to an item and says, "Look! A *flower*." Partner B describes its location, mediating for Partner A. "Yes, it's *near* the *tree*." or "The *river* is *under* the *bridge*." They practice using prepositions and assisting each other to understand spatial relationships with gestures.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "I Can Connect with Nature!".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task: Outdoor Role-Play Explanation (Project 2 Integration).</b> Students, in small groups (3-4), will present their "Outdoor Role-Play" project that they've been developing. The key mediation element for this lesson is that one student from each group will act as the "Explainer" or "Mediator" for their role-play. This student's job is to introduce their group's role-play scenario and explain 2-3 key actions or events to the class or another group, using simple words and gestures to ensure understanding.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">For example, if the role-play is about a picnic in the park:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Explainer says: "Hello! We are in the *park*. We can have a *picnic*!" (gestures eating).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Then, the Explainer describes an action from the role-play, assisting peers: "First, we *walk* (demonstrates walking) *to* the big *tree*. You can *sit* (gestures sitting) *under* the *tree*."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Then, we can *see* a *butterfly* (points and mimics butterfly flying). We can *look* at the *flower* (points)."</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The other group members perform the actions as the Explainer speaks. The teacher circulates, observing the mediation attempts and providing support for clear gestures and simple sentence structures. The focus is on the Explainer's ability to help others understand the scenario and actions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group's designated "mediator" explains one simple sequence (2-3 steps/observations) from their "Outdoor Role-Play" project to the teacher or another student. They must demonstrate their ability to assist peers in following oral directions or understanding simple events using gestures and key words.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Successfully assists peers in understanding nature-related directions/events using gestures.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses at least 3 target vocabulary words (e.g., tree, bird, walk, see, happy).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses "Can/Can't" and simple prepositions of place (e.g., "by the tree", "in the park").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronunciation of /k/ in "can" and /s/ in "sun" is generally clear and intelligible.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration: Actively helps peers follow the explanation.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a simple sentence or draw a picture on a small slip of paper.
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can help my friends understand about nature by _______ (pointing/showing/saying)."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I am happy when I can _______ (e.g., see the sun/hear the birds)."</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy to explain about our nature role-play using your hands and words?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did you learn about helping your friends understand the nature story?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students practice mediation skills at this level (A1.1)? The use of simple gestures and repetitive language seemed effective.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students who struggled to mediate? Perhaps more guided practice with sentence frames for explaining actions and more direct modeling of gestures. Visual cues like picture sequences could also be expanded.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did the project task successfully integrate mediation? Yes, by having a designated "explainer" using gestures and simple words, it targeted the core mediation outcome.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This concludes the unit "I'm Outside. I'm Happy!" and Project 2. The next lesson will introduce a new theme, building upon the foundational communication and social-emotional skills developed in this unit, potentially focusing on "My Family" or "My Community" and basic descriptive language.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>